* The date of Easter in the Gregorian calendar (the anonymous algorithm
* of 1876). JOSS has no remainder function; part 9 is one: r becomes the
* remainder of u divided by v.
1.01 Set u = y.
1.02 Set v = 19.
1.03 Do part 9.
1.04 Set a = r.
1.05 Set b = ip(y/100).
1.06 Set c = y - 100·b.
1.07 Set d = ip(b/4).
1.08 Set e = b - 4·d.
1.09 Set f = ip[(b+8)/25].
1.10 Set g = ip[(b-f+1)/3].
1.11 Set u = 19·a+b-d-g+15.
1.12 Set v = 30.
1.13 Do part 9.
1.14 Set h = r.
1.15 Set i = ip(c/4).
1.16 Set k = c - 4·i.
1.17 Set u = 32+2·e+2·i-h-k.
1.18 Set v = 7.
1.19 Do part 9.
1.20 Set l = r.
1.21 Set m = ip[(a+11·h+22·l)/451].
1.22 Set u = h+l-7·m+114.
1.23 Set v = 31.
1.24 Do part 9.
1.25 Type y, ip(u/31), r+1 in form 1.

9.1 Set r = u - v·ip(u/v).

Form 1:
____   month _   day __

Do part 1 for y = 1964, 1965, 1966, 2000.
